==English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|en|dʰeh₁}}
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|signifier}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|significare}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɪɡ nəˌfaɪ/|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|sig|ni|fy|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|signif|ies}}

# To give (something) a [[meaning]] or an [[importance]].
# To [[show]] one’s [[intention]]s with a [[sign]] etc.
#* {{rfdate}} {{w|William Shakespeare}}
#*: I'll to the king; and '''signify''' to him / That thus I have resign'd my charge to you.
#* {{rfdate}} {{w|Jonathan Swift}}
#*: The government should '''signify''' to the Protestants of Ireland that want of silver is not to be remedied.
# To [[mean]]; to [[betoken]].
#* {{rfdate}} {{w|William Shakespeare}}
#*: A tale / Told by an idiot, full of sound and fury, / '''Signifying''' nothing.

